# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SiestaReport.com : 2026-09-10
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neutral Siesta Key domain shared by Kelli and Ryan (domain alias on this same
# Netlify project; Netlify DNS zone siestareport.com). Host-scoped rules, so
# they fire only on that host and are listed first so the un-scoped /gb rules
# below never shadow them. 200 = the Gulf & Bay page is SERVED at
# SiestaReport.com/GB (URL stays put); the adamsonfl.com URL stays live too and
# keeps the canonical. The bare host serves src/pages/siesta-report/ (Kelli + Ryan
# co-brand). Netlify path matching is case-insensitive, but /GB is
# what is printed, so both spellings are listed for clarity.

https://www.siestareport.com/*  https://siestareport.com/:splat                              301!
# Crawler files for the SiestaReport.com host (2026-10-23). The hub's own robots.txt,
# llms.txt and sitemap were being served here verbatim, telling search engines and AI
# crawlers that this host was adamsonfl.com. Generated under /siesta-report/ by the hub
# build (src/pages/siesta-report/*.ts); forced so the hub's real files never shadow them.
https://siestareport.com/robots.txt         /siesta-report/robots.txt         200!
https://siestareport.com/llms.txt           /siesta-report/llms.txt           200!
https://siestareport.com/sitemap-index.xml  /siesta-report/sitemap-index.xml  200!
https://siestareport.com/sitemap-0.xml      /siesta-report/sitemap-0.xml      200!
# /GBC serves the SiestaReport.com twin of the page (src/pages/siesta-report/gbc.astro:
# SRLayout, no AdamsonFL nav), generated alongside the hub page by gen_gulf_bay_pages.py.
# Renamed from /GB on 2026-09-14; the old path 301s here so the September proofs and any
# QR already in the wild keep landing on the page (ordered BEFORE the /GBC rules because
# Netlify matches top-down and /GB is not a prefix of /GBC, so neither shadows the other).
https://siestareport.com/GB     https://siestareport.com/GBC                                 301!
https://siestareport.com/gb     https://siestareport.com/GBC                                 301!
https://siestareport.com/GB/*   https://siestareport.com/GBC/:splat                          301!
https://siestareport.com/gb/*   https://siestareport.com/GBC/:splat                          301!
https://siestareport.com/GBC    /siesta-report/gbc/                                          200
# /GBC/ is the canonical form (trailing slash, matching every other page and the sitemap);
# listed before the splat rules so it is not read as an empty ?qr= code.
https://siestareport.com/GBC/   /siesta-report/gbc/                                          200
https://siestareport.com/gbc/   /siesta-report/gbc/                                          200
https://siestareport.com/gbc    /siesta-report/gbc/                                          200
https://siestareport.com/GBC/*  /siesta-report/gbc/?qr=:splat&src=typed                      200
https://siestareport.com/gbc/*  /siesta-report/gbc/?qr=:splat&src=typed                      200
# 200! (forced): the hub's own /index.html exists, and an unforced rewrite never shadows a real file.
https://siestareport.com/       /siesta-report/                                              200!
# On the hub host the SiestaReport home has no business being reachable: one public address.
https://adamsonfl.com/siesta-report/gbc  https://siestareport.com/GBC                        301!
https://adamsonfl.com/siesta-report/gbc/ https://siestareport.com/GBC                        301!
https://adamsonfl.com/siesta-report      https://siestareport.com/                           301!
https://adamsonfl.com/siesta-report/*    https://siestareport.com/                           301!

# Printed on the Sept 2026 Gulf & Bay Owner Brief proof before the domain existed.
/gulfbay   https://siestareport.com/GBC?utm_source=mailer&utm_medium=direct-mail&utm_campaign=gb-owner-brief  301

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDX Broker Dynamic Wrapper proxy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Status 200 = proxy (URL stays adamsonfl.com); 301/302 would change the URL.
# IDX serves its own canonical tags so SEO-wise this is the recommended path.

/idx/*           https://adamsonfl.idxbroker.com/idx/:splat              200
/idx             https://adamsonfl.idxbroker.com/idx                     200

# Common IDX paths that don't sit under /idx/ — proxy these too if you use them.
# Uncomment as needed once you've enabled the corresponding features in IDX dashboard.
# /search/*      https://adamsonfl.idxbroker.com/idx/search/:splat        200
# /listings/*    https://adamsonfl.idxbroker.com/idx/results/:splat       200
# /featured/*    https://adamsonfl.idxbroker.com/idx/featured/:splat      200

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Area slug consolidation — 2026-05-19
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lido Key + St. Armands merged into a single area page. The Lido Key polygon
# already covers all of St. Armands Circle and the north-end residential
# streets, so listings from both communities now render on one page.
