# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gulf & Bay Club farm mailer QR / short URLs : 2026-08-14
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-recipient vanity codes: building letter + unit (A=5790, B=5780, C=5770,
# D=5760, E=5750, F=5740). Printed on the Tier 1 postcard as a typed short URL;
# the QR encodes the /gbq/ twin so scans and typed visits separate in analytics.
# ?qr=<CODE> joins back to touch.qr_token -> parcel -> owner.
# 302 (not 301) on purpose: codes are evergreen, destinations may change per issue.
# /gbq/ is listed first; it cannot be shadowed by /gb/* but order makes intent clear.

/gbq/*   /siesta-key/gulf-and-bay-club-beachfront/?qr=:splat&src=scan     302
/gb/*    /siesta-key/gulf-and-bay-club-beachfront/?qr=:splat&src=typed    302
/gb      /siesta-key/gulf-and-bay-club-beachfront/?src=typed              302

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Property folders: 2026-09-16
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One address, one slug. /mkt/<slug>/ is the CMA client page (real folder, wins over these
# rules when it exists). The investment analyzer and its client report are single pages
# served under the same slug via 200 rewrites; the pages read the slug from the path.
/mkt/:slug/invest   /str-dashboard/index.html    200
/mkt/:slug/report   /str-dashboard/report.html   200
# Property home for slugs that have no CMA folder (real folders such as /mkt/admin/ and any
# scaffolded CMA win over these rules automatically). /mkt/ itself is the workspace index.
/mkt/:slug/         /mkt/property.html            200
/mkt/:slug          /mkt/property.html            200

